# Normalise text files to LF, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# This is not cosmetic. Jekyll's default `excerpt_separator` is "\n\n", which
# never matches "\r\n\r\n" — so with CRLF post files, every post's excerpt
# silently resolved to the ENTIRE document. That shipped the full text of each
# post as its <meta name="description"> (23,000+ characters on the TÜDÜM post)
# and as its RSS <summary>.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than plain `text=auto` so the working tree matches what
# GitHub Pages builds from; otherwise excerpts would behave differently in
# local preview than in production.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary assets.
*.png  -text
*.jpg  -text
*.jpeg -text
*.gif  -text
*.avif -text
*.webp -text
*.ico  -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
